            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Currently rustc is called by the `default_sysroot_src` function, which is where this env override takes place.\r\nFor this PR I didn't want to change existing behaviours someone else might depend on or have a mismatch with respect to the error message in case someone does set the `RUSTC` env variable.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/blob/10e9995a8638ad8f72898de3003ef8c686fe6a52/lsp/rust_analyzer.lua#L42-L47",
            "commit_id": "bec6d1c3ff39a2877a222c6e73c77be1e02aef21",
            "created_at": "2026-08-24T13:17:04Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -86,6 +114,10 @@ return {\n   cmd = { 'rust-analyzer' },\n   filetypes = { 'rust' },\n   root_dir = function(bufnr, on_dir)\n+    if not executable_exists('rustc', { env_override = 'RUSTC' }) or not executable_exists('cargo') then",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/pull/4500#discussion_r3843794817",
            "id": 3843794817,
