        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "why do we need to check both rustc *and* cargo? is it actually reasonable for `cargo` to not be installed?\r\n\r\nthe simple, reliable way to address things like https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/issues/4465 is to let `cargo` give the right error message. surely it fails if `rustc` is missing? we shouldn't need to handle env vars like RUSTC; `cargo` should be the one to figure that out.\r\n\r\nso unless i'm missing something, it should be much simpler to just call `cargo` and `notify_once` whatever error it gives. or if it's missing, then we say so.",
